{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And you shall remember that you were a slave in Egypt.</b> In the other festivals there are commandments that one must mention, on account of which Israel went out of Egypt, such as the commandment of matzot on Pesach, sukkah on the Festival of Ingathering, shofar on Rosh HaShanah, fasting on Yom HaKippurim; but Shavuot has no remembrance at all, therefore <b>and you shall remember</b> is written concerning it." "<b>That you were a slave in Egypt.</b> Do not say: how can I abandon the harvest? Rather, remember that you had nothing in your hand when HaShem granted you favor, and you had no leisure to rest and rejoice; therefore <b>and you shall observe and do.</b>"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:53:03.759778497Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}